WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.381
- [Sighing]
Wish y'all would have told me.

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:07.674
I would have got dressed up again.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:09.426
- [Taylor Rooks:] This isn’t dressed up?

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:11.261
- Nah, I wore a bulletproof vest.

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:13.346
You know, I was trying to make a
statement before you got here.
[Phone beeping]

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:16.891
- [Taylor:] Did you really
wear a bulletproof vest?

00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:18.101
Can you show me the vest?

00:00:18.101 --> 00:00:18.935
- Oh.

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:23.189
It has pretty much every
possible name of someone

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.692
who's died from police
brutality, police violence.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.902
On the back too.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.195
Doesn't matter how much
money or how famous you

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.947
are, like, as an
African American male, that's

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:31.781
who we are.

00:00:31.781 --> 00:00:33.908
You know, it doesn't matter
what your job,

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:35.243
what your name is, and
I think being able to

00:00:35.243 --> 00:00:36.953
wear the bulletproof vest just shows that

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.204
I kinda have my hands up as well.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.123
Just kinda like, look, hands up,
don't shoot, you know.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:42.208
We're tired of seeing this.
We're tired. We're tired.

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.043
And everybody's tired of it.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.961
So for me to make that
statement, I think it was

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:47.297
just something that I
really wanted to do and

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.257
I think as African Americans,
male or female, we're

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:51.593
sick and tired of being afraid, you know.

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:54.012
I think that's something
I really want to speak on.

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:59.059
- [Orlando Airport Overhead Announcement:] Welcome to Orlando. The local time is 10:33.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.685
- [Announcer:] Tonight's
presentation of the

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:02.687
national anthem has
been recorded and sung by

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:05.523
a transformational youth organization
in the African American

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:06.941
community.

00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:09.360
- Well we knew we were
gonna be the first game

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.072
and we would have an
opportunity to make a statement.

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:16.409
- The biggest thing was just
finding something we could all do

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.577
together. And I brought it to them,

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.995
and I was like, “Look,
this is what we wanna do.”

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:21.664
And, you know, credit to
everybody that was a part of it.

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:23.249
We appreciate the support.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.252
- It’s a first, and I'm proud
to be part of this league.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.296
- Every day that I'm here,
I get the opportunity to

00:01:28.296 --> 00:01:30.548
hear players talk about things they care

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.592
deeply about.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:35.178
The changes they want to see in the world.

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:36.721
They are so passionate
about so many things.

00:01:36.721 --> 00:01:39.891
It's not just basketball. 
It's really amazing to

00:01:39.891 --> 00:01:40.809
be a part of.

00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:43.353
[Drums, instrumental]

00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:46.189
I love empty buses.
It's a very weird thing,

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:50.151
but I love when I'm the
only person inside of a

00:01:50.151 --> 00:01:52.487
huge vehicle.

00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:54.239
I just wanna scream.

00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:56.407
Next up, Houston Rockets
taking on the

00:01:56.407 --> 00:01:58.493
Memphis Grizzlies.

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:00.578
This will be my first time ever watching

00:02:00.578 --> 00:02:02.205
the Grizzlies in person.
I'm excited to watch

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:03.832
Ja Morant.

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:06.709
- [Announcer:] Game time.

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:08.378
- [Offscreen:] Where are you?

00:02:08.378 --> 00:02:09.504
- Ah, I'm in a bubble

00:02:09.504 --> 00:02:11.756
- [Taylor laughing]

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.344
- Hi, Danny!

00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:18.304
- Hi, how are you?

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:21.850
- Hurry up, LeBron. Whenever you're ready.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.520
- [LeBron James:] I gotta get
some food and some wine.

00:02:28.731 --> 00:02:30.900
[Laughing]

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.696
- [Taylor:] All right, Bron is about be DJ.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:44.581
[Big K.R.I.T.’s “2000 &amp; Beyond” playing]

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:46.624
OK, let's make sure we are framed up.

00:02:46.624 --> 00:02:50.503
- I think that's why it was
important for us to play

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.965
cuz I think at the end of the day,
you know, how now everything is

00:02:53.965 --> 00:02:55.592
so based about social media.

00:02:55.592 --> 00:02:58.261
So something could be the trend

00:02:58.261 --> 00:03:00.054
or, you know, quote, unquote,

00:03:00.054 --> 00:03:03.516
or the wave, like the Black
Lives Matter movement,

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.269
and then three, four months later,
it just starts to

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:07.353
die down.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:10.023
And for us, you know, it's
not gonna hit that three or four

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.108
months and then die down because
we're kinda picking it

00:03:12.108 --> 00:03:15.111
back up, and we continue to raise awareness.

00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:18.156
[Intense violin]

00:03:18.156 --> 00:03:20.992
- Really been so much
unity and conversation

00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:21.993
between players.

00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:24.579
And so now that players
are using their voices,

00:03:24.579 --> 00:03:26.998
it's just about making
sure people are listening

00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:28.917
and still tuning in.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.084
- [Offscreen:] Thank you, Russell.

00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:31.711
- All right, thank you. Appreciate it.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.338
- [Taylor: ] Are those
gonna be for sale?

00:03:33.338 --> 00:03:34.297
- [Russell:] No.

00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:36.382
- [Taylor:] Wow, that's crazy. OK.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.217
- [Russell:] But if you want one, I’ll
get you one.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.509
- [Taylor:] I would love one. I'd love one.

00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:41.221
- [Russell:] Which one do you
want, it to say on the back?

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:43.640
They've got like 10 different ones.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.099
So you just let me know, and I'll get you one.

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:45.934
- [Taylor:] No, I'd love
one. Thank you so much.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:46.768
- [Russell:] I'll bring it Sunday.

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:48.561
- [Taylor] OK, for
sure. I appreciate you.

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.813
- [Russell:] Yep, no problem.

00:03:50.813 --> 00:03:54.192
- [Taylor:] Thank you, Russ.

00:03:54.192 --> 00:03:57.862
[Serious music]

00:04:03.868 --> 00:04:06.621
- All Black people unjustly killed, many

00:04:06.621 --> 00:04:08.873
by the hands of police.

00:04:08.873 --> 00:04:12.919
I chose the back that
says "Power to the people."

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:15.004
- [Taylor:] Hey, Doc.
So, I see your hat

00:04:15.004 --> 00:04:16.047
saying “Vote.”
- Yeah.

00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:18.174
- You guys have a lot of different symbolism

00:04:18.174 --> 00:04:20.677
and signage on the
on the coaches’ shoes, hats and

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:21.970
everything like that.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:24.472
So what have you kind of
learned about yourself

00:04:24.472 --> 00:04:27.100
as a coach during this
time? And what is important

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.186
for you to do for your guys
and for your assistant coaches?

00:04:30.186 --> 00:04:32.230
- Well, for me as a coach,
I've learned two things:

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.066
No. 1, I've always
been extremely political

00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:37.151
but not enough.

00:04:37.151 --> 00:04:42.115
You know. You know, we had
a great speaker recently

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:45.451
talk to our team. And, you know, one of the—
he said, I don't know how anyone

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.912
can say they're not involved in politics

00:04:47.912 --> 00:04:50.456
because politics are
involved your daily lives,

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.625
whether you want it or not.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:54.377
Decisions are being made whether you're

00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:55.295
involved or not.

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.213
So why wouldn't you be
involved? That's the

00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:58.214
first thing.

00:04:58.214 --> 00:05:00.633
And the second thing, I hate to say it—

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.386
I think I'm getting
old, and I think I should listen

00:05:03.386 --> 00:05:05.930
to the young people. You know,

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:10.935
I think this movement is
really driven by the young.

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:15.064
And so my job is to
inspire them to vote and

00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:17.608
get involved and then
back up and let them do

00:05:17.608 --> 00:05:19.360
the talking and us do the listening.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.696
I think that's very
important in this movement

00:05:21.696 --> 00:05:23.740
And if we can do that, then
we don't just have young

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:27.702
people involved in politics
now but we have people

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:29.746
involved in politics for life.

00:05:29.746 --> 00:05:31.622
And I think that's very important for us.

00:05:31.622 --> 00:05:35.626
- Game 1. It has arrived.
The NBA has returned.

00:05:35.626 --> 00:05:38.129
We're tipping off with the
Jazz taking on the Pelicans.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:41.299
Zion Williamson is playing.
He's back on campus.

00:05:41.299 --> 00:05:44.844
I can't wait. I have waited
for this day. Let's do it.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.430
[Squeaking shoes and whistle blowing]

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:51.392
[Upbeat music]

00:05:51.392 --> 00:05:54.228
[Squeaking shoes and whistle blowing]

00:05:57.065 --> 00:05:59.734
[Basketball bouncing]

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.695
- [Taylor:] We can't touch it. I'm sorry.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:06.783
[Upbeat music]

00:06:06.783 --> 00:06:09.035
[Laughing]

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:14.499
- I truly believe that
us as athletes have a

00:06:14.499 --> 00:06:16.834
huge platform. Because us as people

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.586
have platforms that we
all can use to be able to give back

00:06:18.586 --> 00:06:19.879
to our community,

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.840
to be able to educate
our people. And that's

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:25.635
something I believe
in, something I've been

00:06:25.635 --> 00:06:27.345
doing since Day 1.

00:06:27.345 --> 00:06:29.430
And I'll continue to do it
to be able to bridge and close

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.264
that gap.

00:06:32.016 --> 00:06:33.101
And that's just how I feel.

00:06:33.101 --> 00:06:38.064
- I don't think that, you know,
kneeling or putting on a

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:40.942
T-shirt for me personally is the answer.

00:06:40.942 --> 00:06:44.153
I feel like, for me, Black
lives are supported through

00:06:44.153 --> 00:06:45.029
the gospel.

00:06:45.029 --> 00:06:47.657
All lives are supported
through the gospel. That we

00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:48.491
all,

00:06:48.491 --> 00:06:50.660
like I said, have
things that we do wrong

00:06:51.536 --> 00:06:53.121
and sometimes it gets
to a place of pointing

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:55.623
fingers about which wrong is worse.

00:06:55.623 --> 00:06:57.875
And whose wrong is seen, so

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:00.628
I feel like the Bible tells us that
we all fall short of

00:07:00.628 --> 00:07:05.633
God's glory. And that at the end of the day
whoever will humble themselves

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:11.097
and seek God and repent their sins,
that we could see

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.306
it in a different light.

00:07:13.182 --> 00:07:15.143
- I'm happy I'm getting you
with the pick in your hair.

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:16.227
It looks nice.

00:07:16.227 --> 00:07:17.520
- You don't see what's
on the pick, do you?

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.604
Because it's backwards.

00:07:20.648 --> 00:07:21.858
- [Offscreen:] What is it?

00:07:21.858 --> 00:07:24.694
- Oh, there we go. It
is power to the people.

00:07:24.694 --> 00:07:25.528
Do you see the pick?

00:07:25.528 --> 00:07:26.654
Where'd you get that?

00:07:26.654 --> 00:07:28.698
- I don't know. Amazon. Six dollars.

00:07:30.199 --> 00:07:31.033
- A steal.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.163
- Yeah, definitely.
It's an amazing feeling
to see how far we've

00:07:36.205 --> 00:07:40.042
come and we still have so
much more to go, you know?

00:07:40.042 --> 00:07:42.712
But it's an amazing feeling to see that we are

00:07:42.712 --> 00:07:45.214
taking steps in a positive direction.

00:07:46.591 --> 00:07:48.426
We just gotta remember
that it's not finished.

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:49.802
The job isn't done yet.

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:52.221
We just gotta continue
to do what we can to

00:07:52.221 --> 00:07:54.849
use our platform to let
everyone know that this

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:56.976
is something that's not
temporary, you know?

00:07:56.976 --> 00:07:59.270
This is something that
we will continue to do

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:00.730
until we are answered.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.190
- [Taylor:] What is it that you would like to see

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.858
from the owners that
would make you feel like

00:08:03.858 --> 00:08:04.984
they get it?

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:08.237
- Just some acknowledgement.
I think that's a huge part

00:08:08.237 --> 00:08:09.572
of taking some ownership.

00:08:11.073 --> 00:08:13.910
That, you know, half our league, I mean,

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:16.454
80 percent of our league
is African American men.

00:08:17.622 --> 00:08:21.501
And they need to make sure
that they voice that to us

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:24.253
show their concerns show
that they're supporting

00:08:24.253 --> 00:08:25.630
the things we want to do

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.882
for our communities, for our people.

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:30.134
Especially now more than ever.

00:08:30.134 --> 00:08:32.637
It's something that I think
is very, very important.

00:08:32.637 --> 00:08:35.431
especially you know owners
should take knowledge

00:08:35.431 --> 00:08:36.265
of that.

00:08:36.265 --> 00:08:37.433
- [Taylor:] Finish this sentence for me.

00:08:37.433 --> 00:08:39.852
Black people are:

00:08:39.852 --> 00:08:40.978
- Probably just "beautiful."

00:08:40.978 --> 00:08:44.982
I think, you know, obviously, that
goes much more into,

00:08:44.982 --> 00:08:47.818
much more in depth than just the physical.

00:08:47.818 --> 00:08:51.781
You know, mentally, I think
we're a brilliant race,

00:08:51.781 --> 00:08:53.199
who's smart, you know,

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:58.204
who don't get
its just due. You know, obviously, but.

00:09:00.373 --> 00:09:03.209
We're a race who's just beautiful.

00:09:04.544 --> 00:09:06.879
- [Taylor:] So, Chris, I know
you guys want awareness

00:09:06.879 --> 00:09:09.465
and you want change. But
once this Orlando campus

00:09:10.508 --> 00:09:11.842
has finished, what will have to have happened

00:09:11.842 --> 00:09:14.971
for you to say, "We were successful in that"?

00:09:14.971 --> 00:09:16.722
- That's a great question.
That's a great question.

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.892
I think the more we all
continue to get educated,

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:20.893
you know, what I mean?

00:09:20.893 --> 00:09:23.854
And coming down here, what
we have the opportunity to do

00:09:23.854 --> 00:09:26.691
is use our collective
voices, obviously to spread

00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:28.693
the message, but we also
get a chance to educate

00:09:28.693 --> 00:09:30.695
each other. With whatever it may be.

00:09:30.695 --> 00:09:35.408
Whether it's financial
literacy. Whether it is

00:09:35.408 --> 00:09:38.035
police reform. Whether it is
education. Whether it's

00:09:38.035 --> 00:09:39.412
HBCUs.

00:09:39.412 --> 00:09:41.163
Guys can start to build together.

00:09:41.163 --> 00:09:44.041
That's what we've been
talking about. We need to,

00:09:44.041 --> 00:09:46.168
we need to unite,
become a united force

00:09:46.168 --> 00:09:48.212
in a lot of this action that's going on, so.

00:09:49.338 --> 00:09:51.090
I'm not the one to
determine this, but it's just

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:53.092
things that I like to see.

00:09:54.302 --> 00:09:55.970
- [Donovan Mitchell:] The
game was great. We won by two.

00:09:56.929 --> 00:09:57.763
But at the end of the day,
Breonna Taylor's killers

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:59.181
are still free.

00:09:59.181 --> 00:10:00.016
There are so many different
things that we can honestly

00:10:00.016 --> 00:10:01.058
talk about.

00:10:01.058 --> 00:10:02.768
I'm gonna continue to
talk about Breonna Taylor.

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:04.145
That's near and dear to me.

00:10:04.145 --> 00:10:05.980
I'm gonna keep it on the
forefront of people's minds.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.316
You know, and I think they wanted to
do something as well and

00:10:08.316 --> 00:10:09.942
just being able to bring
that to them and being able

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:12.612
to do it, just showed
how collectively as a group

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:14.864
and as a league we're going to
continue to keep that

00:10:14.864 --> 00:10:16.240
on everybody's minds.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:17.950
- [Taylor:] LeBron, you
talked about what you want

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.202
next for Breonna Taylor
in terms of justice.

00:10:20.202 --> 00:10:22.955
But what do you want
next in terms of us, in

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.040
terms of Americans?

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:26.876
What does an improved
America look like to you?

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:30.296
- I mean, that's a great question.

00:10:30.296 --> 00:10:34.842
And it's something that I
rationalize and think about

00:10:34.842 --> 00:10:35.718
every single day.

00:10:36.594 --> 00:10:37.720
You know, what's next?

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.680
What can I do next to
make an impact in our

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:40.514
communities?

00:10:41.515 --> 00:10:43.851
You know, not only for my people, but also

00:10:43.851 --> 00:10:45.311
for America in general.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.981
You know obviously
justice for Breonna Taylor

00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:51.233
is No. 1 on all
of our lists right now

00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:54.320
because we just, we know the story, we know

00:10:55.821 --> 00:11:00.785
how…it's just crazy what went
on with that situation

00:11:00.785 --> 00:11:01.786
and how horrific it is.

00:11:01.786 --> 00:11:06.624
So, but for us as America,
to get better? That's

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.293
a question we kinda tinker with every day.

00:11:09.293 --> 00:11:11.545
And it's something I play
with in my mind every day

00:11:11.545 --> 00:11:14.465
and listen to the people
around me and also listen

